dialogue trust_knight_1
title: Words on the rim
trigger: Trust knight level=1
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The camp is asleep except for the Knight, who sits by the coals with the shield face down across both knees, working a whetstone round the inside of the rim.
  * You'll wear that rim through before the Captain ever gets a swing at it. -> rim
    do: AddTrust $with -2
  * You took the worst of it today. Let me see the arm. -> arm
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * Mind if I sit up with you a while? -> sit
    do: AddTrust $with 4

node rim hero
  It won't wear through. Hold iron's thicker than Choir iron. I'm not sharpening it, anyway. I'm cleaning the words.
  -> words

node arm hero
  The arm's fine. Bruised, that's all. A shield arm's meant to be bruised. Sit, if you like. I'm cleaning the words.
  -> words

node sit hero
  Sit. The fire's better with two. You can watch me clean the words, if that's your idea of company.
  -> words

node words commander
  The Knight tilts the shield to the coals. Cut into the inside of the rim, worn smooth in places by a thumb, runs a single line of old hold script.
  -> oath

node oath hero
  Stand before the hold, and the hold stands. Every squire cuts it into the first shield they carry. You say it in the hall, with your hand on the iron and the whole hold watching.
  -> hall

node hall hero
  The Captain stood at the front of the hall the night I swore it. Nodded at every word. Then the same night, the tithe went up the beam, and the Captain went back to counting.
  -> doubt

node doubt hero
  So here's what keeps me sitting up, Commander. I swore it in the Captain's hall, in front of the Captain. If the Captain's sold the hold, what's left of the oath? Who am I standing in front of now?
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The whetstone stops. The Knight waits, thumb resting on the first word.
  * The oath was to the hold, not the hall. The people are still there. So is the oath. -> people
    do: AddTrust $with 9
    do: SetFlag knight:oath_people
  * Keep it until you know for certain. An oath shouldn't be put down in the dark. -> kept
    do: AddTrust $with 5
    do: SetFlag knight:oath_kept
  * The Captain broke it first. You owe that oath nothing now. Scratch it out. -> cut
    do: AddTrust $with -4
    do: SetFlag knight:oath_cut

node people hero
  The hold, not the hall. My sister's in that hold. The old smith who made this rim. The children who carry water up from the well. I never once swore anything to the Captain. I just thought I had.
  -> close_line

node kept hero
  Not in the dark. That's fair. That's how my teacher would have said it. I'll carry it a while longer, then, and see where it points.
  -> close_line

node cut hero
  Scratch it out. Easy to say when it isn't cut into your own iron. I won't. If I do that, I'm just a hammer somebody's pointing. I'll keep it, Commander, even if you think it's spent.
  -> close_line

node close_line hero
  Go on and sleep. Somebody has to be the first thing in front of the wagon in the morning, and it's me.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Knight turns the shield over, face out, and leans it against the wagon wheel where the first light will catch it.
